Template: homelab-pgbouncer/listen_addr
Type: string
Default: *
Description: Address for pgbouncer to listen on:
 '*' for all interfaces, or a specific IP.

Template: homelab-pgbouncer/listen_port
Type: string
Default: 6432
Description: Port for pgbouncer to listen on:

Template: homelab-pgbouncer/pool_mode
Type: select
Choices: session, transaction, statement
Default: session
Description: Pooling mode:
 session is the safest default for clients using long-lived connections
 and/or server-side prepared statements (e.g. Perl DBD::Pg, most ORMs).
 transaction/statement pool more aggressively but break those clients --
 only choose them if every connecting app is known to be compatible.

Template: homelab-pgbouncer/postgres_host
Type: string
Default:
Description: Postgres host backing the shared 'homelab' database:
 Address of the homelab-database host this pgbouncer will front.
 Required -- config generation is skipped until this is set.

Template: homelab-pgbouncer/postgres_port
Type: string
Default: 5432
Description: Postgres port backing the shared 'homelab' database:

Template: homelab-pgbouncer/admin_users
Type: string
Default:
Description: Comma-separated pgbouncer admin users (optional):
 Users allowed to connect to pgbouncer's special "pgbouncer" admin
 database (SHOW POOLS, RELOAD, etc). Leave blank to skip.
